This file is /mmi-cad/src/logic_generators/0README

Welcome to the logic generators.  These generators run under sue/dpc,
and produce a variety of (hopefully correct) logic elements.

These are the files in this directory:

RevHistory*		: detailed rev history for every generator
mmig_AND/		: generates wider and stronger AND/NANDs than are in the MMI library
mmig_AOn1/		: generates wider and stronger AOn1/AOIn1s than are in the MMI library
mmig_MUX/		: generates wider and stronger MUX/MUXIs than are in the MMI library
mmig_OR/		: generates wider and stronger OR/NORs than are in the MMI library
mmig_adder/		: generates carry select or ripple adders
mmig_comparator/	: generates zero detectors and comparators
mmig_decode/		: generates binary decoders
mmig_fastqueue/		: generates fast but small depth queues
mmig_mul/		: generates multipliers
mmig_mul_array/		: part of mmig_mul: generates 4:2 multiplier arrays
mmig_mul_ppg_array/	: orphaned code, was part of older versions of mmig_mul
mmig_mul_ppg_slice/	: part of mmig_ppg: generates one bitslice of ppg logic
mmig_mul_slice/		: part of mmig_mul_array: generates one bitslice of mul array
mmig_nandbuf/		: part of mmig_ppg: generates nandbuf structures
mmig_partshifter/	: orphaned code, an attempt at a partitioned shifter
mmig_ppg/		: part of mmig_mul: partial product generation
mmig_ppg_4bit/		: part of mmig_ppg_slice: partial produce generation for 4 bits
mmig_ppg_booth/		: part of mmig_mul: booth recoder for multiplier
mmig_ppg_slice/		: part of mmig_ppg: generates one bitslice of mmig_ppg
mmig_queue/		: generates deeper & slower queues (FIFOs) than mmig_fastqueue
mmig_shifter/		: generates shifters and rotators
mmig_stack/		: generates stacks (LIFOs)
mmig_testCounter/	: generates test counter structure, used in testing schematics
release1.0/		: release used for Malleable .25um tapeouts
release_latest/		: latest release
utilities/		: utility routines used by many generators

===============================================================================================
Some of the generators run standalone, some must be called by other generators.
The standalone generators can be placed in a schematic by a designer, the rest
can only be instantiated by higher level generators.  The standalone (top level)
generators are:

mmig_AND
mmig_AOn1
